bo 1
# The standard library of Bo, edition 1: the core's built-in actions, which
# hand a thing over and suspend, resume, end, or cancel it. The vocabulary
# packs bring their own (bo/stdlib/finance.bo, bo/stdlib/services.bo). A
# contract that writes `can transfer to buyer` gets the transfer below, with
# the buyer as its counterparty; the lines the contract writes under
# `can transfer` add to it and are checked first. Without `to`, each call
# names the counterparty (R21). To change a built-in action, copy it under a
# name of your own: `cexchain bo stdlib show transfer` prints it, in any
# language.
#
# The fields these terms use: holder (a party). An action can start only from
# the states its terms name; a state the contract never reaches is left out.
# A time rule may do any of these actions that names no counterparty and
# takes no inputs, as the contract's own word (R24).

# The holder hands the thing over: the counterparty becomes its holder. Both
# consent to every transfer, the holder by starting it (the counterparty by
# R3, R21, or R31). Only an active thing is handed over (so not while
# pledged, under the finance pack).
can transfer to counterparty by holder
  requires not counterparty = holder
  active -> active
  holder = counterparty

# The holder cancels the thing.
can cancel by holder
  active -> cancelled

# The home suspends the instance on its own word, such as when it is overdue
# (when overdue 3 days suspend).
can suspend
  active -> suspended

# The home resumes a suspended instance.
can resume
  suspended -> active

# The home ends the instance, active or suspended: nothing can start from
# terminated.
can terminate
  active, suspended -> terminated
